# Windows batch scripts must always be checked out with CRLF, regardless of whatever
# core.autocrlf a given clone happens to have configured (or lacks entirely, e.g. on Linux/Mac).
# A LF-only .bat file can silently corrupt cmd.exe's parsing of multi-line if/for (...) blocks —
# see docs/DECISIONS.md's 2026-08-11 entry for a real repro of this exact bug in
# packaging/setup.bat.
*.bat text eol=crlf
